<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shah Shuja (Muzaffarid)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1358">1358</a>–<a href="/years/1384">1384</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shah Shuja was ruler of the Muzaffarid dynasty in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from 1358 to 1384, after deposing and blinding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mubariz-al-din-muhammad">Mubariz al-Din Muhammad</a>. His court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> was a centre of Persian culture, where the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafez">Hafez</a> enjoyed his favour. His reign was disturbed by wars with his brothers and relatives and with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalayirid-sultanate">Jalayirids</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shah-shuja-muzaffarid.jpg" alt="Shah Shuja (Muzaffarid)" width="320" height="507" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1592 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_between_Muzaffarid_Shah_Shuja_(detail)_and_his_brother_Mahmud._Khvandamir,_%E1%B8%A4ab%C4%ABbu%CA%BEs-Siyar,_1592._Istanbul,_S%C3%BCleymaniye_K%C3%BCt%C3%BCphanesi,_Hekimo%C4%9Flu_Ali_Pa%C5%9Fa,_738,_fol._155r.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
